{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the cubic polynomial \\( p(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d \\) given the conditions \\( p(-3) = -6 \\), \\( p(4) = 8 \\), \\( p(5) = 10 \\), and \\( p(7) = 15 \\), we can use the fact that \\( p(x) - (x+2) \\) is a cubic polynomial with roots at \\( x = -3, 4, 5, 7 \\). This means that \\( p(x) - (x+2) = k(x+3)(x-4)(x-5)(x-7) \\). However, since \\( p(x) \\) is a cubic polynomial, the term \\( k(x+3)(x-4)(x-5)(x-7) \\) must be a quadratic polynomial, which implies \\( k = 0 \\). Therefore, we can write \\( p(x) = x + 2 \\).\n\nTo verify, we check the given conditions:\n1. \\( p(-3) = -3 + 2 = -1 \\neq -6 \\)\n2. \\( p(4) = 4 + 2 = 6 \\neq 8 \\)\n3. \\( p(5) = 5 + 2 = 7 \\neq 10 \\)\n4. \\( p(7) = 7 + 2 = 9 \\neq 15 \\)\n\n","prefix_end":690,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,40899,47311,17767,281,2075,8,284,3859,61,18,488,44241,61,17,488,20716,488,294,1124,8,2661,279,4682,17767,281,4080,18,8,284,481,21,1124,701,17767,281,7,19,8,284,220,23,1124,701,17767,281,7,20,8,284,220,16,15,1124,701,323,17767,281,7,22,8,284,220,16,20,1124,701,582,646,990,279,2097,429,17767,281,2075,8,481,320,87,10,17,8,1124,8,374,264,40899,47311,448,19703,518,17767,856,284,481,18,11,220,19,11,220,20,11,220,22,1124,568,1096,3363,429,17767,281,2075,8,481,320,87,10,17,8,284,595,2075,10,18,2376,87,12,19,2376,87,12,20,2376,87,12,22,8,1124,568,4354,11,2474,17767,281,2075,8,1124,8,374,264,40899,47311,11,279,4647,17767,595,2075,10,18,2376,87,12,19,2376,87,12,20,2376,87,12,22,8,1124,8,1969,387,264,79151,47311,11,892,23945,17767,595,284,220,15,1124,568,15277,11,582,646,3270,17767,281,2075,8,284,856,488,220,17,1124,3593,1249,10146,11,582,1779,279,2661,4682,510,16,13,17767,281,4080,18,8,284,481,18,488,220,17,284,481,16,1124,811,80,481,21,1124,340,17,13,17767,281,7,19,8,284,220,19,488,220,17,284,220,21,1124,811,80,220,23,1124,340,18,13,177